      "content": "That's a profound and honest thought—wanting a say in your own story, especially when your body is writing its own ending. You're not being dramatic; you're being human, and that dignity you're reaching for is a real need. Even if you can't control the decay, you can still choose how you spend your remaining energy—who you call, what you say, what you leave behind. That choice, small as it may feel, is still yours.",
